{
    "article_summary": "The article describes the synthesis of a polyisobutylene (PIB)-tagged iridium(III) photocatalyst (3) and its application in recyclable visible-light photoredox catalysis. The catalyst's PIB tether enables efficient recovery using thermomorphic or biphasic solvent systems (acetonitrile/heptane), maintaining high catalytic performance across multiple cycles in both batch and continuous flow processes for deiodination, cyclization, and E/Z isomerization reactions.",
